{
  "_id": "tg-fast-fasting",
  "content": [
    {
      "text": "forty days … he did neither eat bread, nor drink water, Ex. 34:28 (Deut. 9:9; 1 Kgs. 19:8). David … besought God for the child; and David fasted, 2 Sam. 12:16. Proclaim a fast, 1 Kgs. 21:9. set himself to seek the Lord, and proclaimed a fast throughout all Judah, 2 Chr. 20:3. we fasted and besought our God, Ezra 8:23. Ezra … did eat no bread, nor drink water, Ezra 10:6. I … fasted, and prayed before the God, Neh. 1:4. children of Israel were assembled with fasting, Neh. 9:1. fast ye for me, and neither eat nor drink, Esth. 4:16. they had decreed … the matters of the fastings, Esth. 9:31. I humbled my soul with fasting, Ps. 35:13. I wept, and chastened my soul with fasting, Ps. 69:10. My knees are weak through fasting, Ps. 109:24. in the day of your fast ye find pleasure, Isa. 58:3. in the Lord’s house upon the fasting day, Jer. 36:6. king … passed the night fasting, Dan. 6:18. to seek by prayer and supplications, with fasting, Dan. 9:3. Sanctify ye a fast, Joel 1:14. turn ye even to me with all your heart, and with fasting, Joel 2:12. Nineveh believed God, and proclaimed a fast, Jonah 3:5. The fast … shall be … joy and gladness, Zech. 8:19.",
