    {
      "text": "when he had fasted forty days and forty nights, Matt. 4:2 (Luke 4:2). appear not unto men to fast, Matt. 6:18 (3 Ne. 13:16). bridegroom shall be taken … then shall they fast, Matt. 9:15 (Mark 2:20). not send them away fasting, Matt. 15:32 (Mark 8:3). this kind goeth not out but by prayer and fasting, Matt. 17:21. come forth by nothing, but by prayer and fasting, Mark 9:29. a widow … served God with fastings and prayers, Luke 2:37. Can ye make the children … fast, Luke 5:34. I fast twice in the week, Luke 18:12. Four days ago I was fasting, Acts 10:30. they ministered to the Lord, and fasted, Acts 13:2. ordained them elders … and had prayed with fasting, Acts 14:23. because the fast was now already past, Acts 27:9. fourteenth day … continued fasting, Acts 27:33. give yourselves to fasting and prayer, 1 Cor. 7:5. hunger and thirst, in fastings, 2 Cor. 11:27.",
